      "message": "fix(sim): the envelope vertical-rapid sweep keeps the lift-out-of-the-kerf rule\n\n#4108 (#4062) sweeps the vertical rapids of an Envelope path against the\npart with the whole cutter at the start pose. A retract that starts at the\nend of a finishing feed starts in that cut's pose, where the finish law\nlets the edge touch the model by the finish tolerance. Each such retract\nwas refused as RapidInPart, and motion's finish3d_hop_height went red.\n\nAn upward vertical rapid that starts where a cut ended now takes the\nstack_hits rule: the shank and holder are swept over the rapid, and the\nedge is judged by the column it rises into. The canopy retracts of #4062\nstay refused.\n\nFixes #4211\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
